507
00:25:07,914 --> 00:25:09,778
- One of our dwarves died.

508
00:25:09,813 --> 00:25:11,849
- Mister Cooper.

509
00:25:11,884 --> 00:25:13,333
I may have something for you

510
00:25:13,368 --> 00:25:15,853
that will provide
the proof you seek.

511
00:25:15,888 --> 00:25:18,200
- Oh yeah?

512
00:25:19,546 --> 00:25:22,308
- It's a pie from
Baker's Square.

513
00:25:23,965 --> 00:25:26,622
- Looks like an old book.
- Do do do do do do!

514
00:25:26,657 --> 00:25:29,591
- Oh, that it
is, Mister Cooper.

515
00:25:29,625 --> 00:25:32,525
It's a book of magic.
- With a pop-o-matic.

516
00:25:32,559 --> 00:25:37,392
- My own compilation of
spells and incantations.

517
00:25:37,426 --> 00:25:39,532
- More talk of magic?

518
00:25:39,566 --> 00:25:42,155
I told you the only kind
of magic I believe in

519
00:25:42,190 --> 00:25:43,847
is the magic I have
in these fingers

520
00:25:43,881 --> 00:25:46,884
to make this place [snaps
fingers] disappear.

521
00:25:46,919 --> 00:25:50,163
- Mister Cooper, if you
would just take this book home

522
00:25:50,198 --> 00:25:53,166
and read through
it, I assure you,

523
00:25:53,201 --> 00:25:56,100
you will be
thoroughly satisfied.

524
00:25:56,135 --> 00:25:58,551
- I'm sure you will
find that it makes

525
00:25:58,585 --> 00:26:01,105
- Do do do do do do...
- good reading.

526
00:26:01,140 --> 00:26:02,935
- It's on the Oprah list.

527
00:26:02,969 --> 00:26:05,903
- All right, you've sparked
my interest, old man.

528
00:26:05,938 --> 00:26:08,009
I'll look through it.

529
00:26:08,043 --> 00:26:10,425
And you'll trust me
to bring it back?

530
00:26:10,459 --> 00:26:11,771
- Why, certainly.

531
00:26:11,806 --> 00:26:13,877
Oh, Missus Cooper,
- You're fine!

532
00:26:13,911 --> 00:26:16,465
- Please, keep the stone.

533
00:26:16,500 --> 00:26:17,708
- Oh, no, I couldn't.

534
00:26:17,743 --> 00:26:19,814
- Dear, it's a gift.

535
00:26:19,848 --> 00:26:22,851
- Have some slightly
used dress shields, too.

536
00:26:22,886 --> 00:26:24,335
- Thank you.

537
00:26:24,370 --> 00:26:26,303
- You're welcome!
- You're welcome.

538
00:26:26,337 --> 00:26:27,822
- Come on, let's
get outta here.

539
00:26:27,856 --> 00:26:29,582
I'm sure the
compilations of a mad man

540
00:26:29,616 --> 00:26:31,826
will make good reading.

541
00:26:31,860 --> 00:26:34,345
- Oh, and Mister Cooper.
- You're welcome.

542
00:26:34,380 --> 00:26:36,658
- A few words of caution.

543
00:26:36,692 --> 00:26:39,281
If you decide to dabble
with any of my spells,

544
00:26:39,316 --> 00:26:42,319
for whatever reason,
- You're welcome!

545
00:26:42,353 --> 00:26:44,493
- Be sure not to toy
- [laughs] Do it again!

546
00:26:44,528 --> 00:26:47,151
- with any that
aren't entirely there.

547
00:26:47,186 --> 00:26:49,015
- You insulting my sperm count?

548
00:26:49,050 --> 00:26:52,122
- I'm afraid that
over the years,

549
00:26:52,156 --> 00:26:55,021
some of the pages
have become brittle.

550
00:26:55,056 --> 00:26:56,264
- Like the missus, here.

551
00:26:56,298 --> 00:26:59,025
- And sections have...

552
00:27:00,026 --> 00:27:03,374
broken off.
- Again like the missus here.

553
00:27:03,409 --> 00:27:06,101
- So please, Mister Cooper,

554
00:27:06,136 --> 00:27:10,140
heed my words.
- Munch my shorts.

555
00:27:10,174 --> 00:27:12,625
- For your own sake.

556
00:27:12,659 --> 00:27:15,559
- Look, my reviews have
destroyed whole cities.

557
00:27:15,593 --> 00:27:17,941
[doors clang shut]

558
00:27:27,053 --> 00:27:28,468
- Yeah, so anyway, Mike,

559
00:27:28,503 --> 00:27:31,333
it's clear that niche reviewing
is the wave of the future.

560
00:27:31,368 --> 00:27:32,472
- Mmhmm.

561
00:27:32,507 --> 00:27:33,577
- The ugly guy in the
movie reviews novelty stores

562
00:27:33,611 --> 00:27:36,373
and CD strip malls,
and he's famous!

563
00:27:36,407 --> 00:27:39,100
- Yeah, so we figured
why not review each other?

564
00:27:39,134 --> 00:27:40,480
- Yeah.
[Servo laughs]

565
00:27:40,515 --> 00:27:41,999
- It'll tell the world
about our delightful selves,

566
00:27:42,034 --> 00:27:44,657
which needs to happen,
and we become famous.

567
00:27:44,691 --> 00:27:46,797
- I'll go first.
[clears throat]

568
00:27:46,832 --> 00:27:48,903
From the moment I saw Tom Servo,

569
00:27:48,937 --> 00:27:52,527
I was taken with his gay,
even naughty bright red color.

570
00:27:52,561 --> 00:27:55,219
And the unexpected,
clear Pyrex dome.

571
00:27:55,254 --> 00:27:58,740
The little dangly arms, though
the function was unclear,

572
00:27:58,774 --> 00:28:01,950
added to the lighthearted
feel of the experience.

573
00:28:01,985 --> 00:28:03,883
Flawless? No.

574
00:28:03,918 --> 00:28:06,472
But I recommend this
Tom Servo for children,

575
00:28:06,506 --> 00:28:09,337
and anyone looking for a
bare bones kinda robot.

576
00:28:09,371 --> 00:28:11,235
There you go.

577
00:28:11,270 --> 00:28:12,443
- Huh.

578
00:28:12,478 --> 00:28:14,411
My turn? Good.
[clears throat]

579
00:28:14,445 --> 00:28:15,584
Everyone's talking about the new

580
00:28:15,619 --> 00:28:17,966
Crow T. Robot out
on Highway Six.

581
00:28:18,001 --> 00:28:19,278
Insouciant, ecclectic,

582
00:28:19,312 --> 00:28:21,797
it seems to promise
a kind of excitement.

583
00:28:21,832 --> 00:28:25,249
Yet the overall effect becomes
rather more garish than fun,

584
00:28:25,284 --> 00:28:28,977
and I left feeling
altogether empty and sad.

585
00:28:29,012 --> 00:28:31,393
- Well, seems like you
guys are on your way

586
00:28:31,428 --> 00:28:33,395
with the whole niche
reviewing thing, so...

587
00:28:33,430 --> 00:28:34,845
- Hey, hold on, Mike,
hold on, hold on.

588
00:28:34,880 --> 00:28:36,640
My second visit to Tom Servo

589
00:28:36,674 --> 00:28:38,884
was even a greater
disappointment.

590
00:28:38,918 --> 00:28:40,264
Loud and overpriced,
- What?

591
00:28:40,299 --> 00:28:43,060
- There was a thick, oily
film coating every surface,

592
00:28:43,095 --> 00:28:44,682
and I can only hope I escaped

593
00:28:44,717 --> 00:28:46,167
with no serious disease.

594
00:28:46,201 --> 00:28:47,858
- If my readers
responses are any guide,

595
00:28:47,893 --> 00:28:50,585
the Crow T. Robot era
is coming to a close.

596
00:28:50,619 --> 00:28:52,552
This poorly conceived disaster

597
00:28:52,587 --> 00:28:54,554
is revealed now as
a spindly testament

598
00:28:54,589 --> 00:28:56,936
to poor taste and nausea.

599
00:28:56,971 --> 00:28:58,179
- The verdict is in,

600
00:28:58,213 --> 00:29:01,216
and the world was not awaiting
a chubby, pompous eunuch!

601
00:29:01,251 --> 00:29:02,493
- What do you mean, chubby?
- Uh, we'll let these guys

602
00:29:02,528 --> 00:29:04,323
sort it out, we'll
be right back.

603
00:29:04,357 --> 00:29:05,186
- I'll give you chubby.

604
00:29:05,220 --> 00:29:06,256
Goodbye, Crow T. Robot.

605
00:29:06,290 --> 00:29:07,705
Your ghastly memory
- Pathetic, ugly,

606
00:29:07,740 --> 00:29:09,017
overbearing and stupid...
- still pollutes my mind.

607
00:29:09,052 --> 00:29:11,709
[upbeat pop music]

608
00:29:31,971 --> 00:29:35,630
- And so, Mister Cooper
took Merlin's book home...

609
00:29:35,664 --> 00:29:36,665
- Wait a minute.

610
00:29:36,700 --> 00:29:37,666
What did Madeline wish for?

611
00:29:37,701 --> 00:29:38,702
[Mike and Robots laugh]
- What?

612
00:29:38,736 --> 00:29:39,599
- What do you think?

613
00:29:39,634 --> 00:29:41,049
- I don't know.

614
00:29:41,084 --> 00:29:44,639
- You'll figure it out.
- Are you Susie's boy?

615
00:29:47,745 --> 00:29:51,439
- Well, let's go
make love, I guess.

616
00:29:52,958 --> 00:29:54,545
- I spoke to Doctor Collins.

617
00:29:54,580 --> 00:29:56,271
- Oh yeah? What'd
that quack have to say?

618
00:29:56,306 --> 00:29:58,584
- He blamed your weiner.
- Nothing.

619
00:29:58,618 --> 00:30:00,896
Nothing that would concern you.

620
00:30:00,931 --> 00:30:02,864
- Oh, for Pete's
sake, Madeline.

621
00:30:02,898 --> 00:30:04,003
- Why is it so
difficult for you

622
00:30:04,038 --> 00:30:06,109
to show a little
compassion once in awhile?

623
00:30:06,143 --> 00:30:07,489
Or to be nice?

624
00:30:07,524 --> 00:30:10,113
My God, just getting along
is a major accomplishment.

625
00:30:10,147 --> 00:30:13,150
- Yeah.
- Whew.

626
00:30:13,185 --> 00:30:16,982
If she had a store,
I'd crush her.

627
00:30:17,016 --> 00:30:20,640
- All right, how do you
get outta this thing?

628
00:30:20,675 --> 00:30:22,159
- Well, it would
appear that I, too,

629
00:30:22,194 --> 00:30:24,299
have succumbed to
the old man's charm,

630
00:30:24,334 --> 00:30:27,475
for I hold in my hand
a book of spells.

631
00:30:27,509 --> 00:30:29,442
Merlin's book of spells,

632
00:30:29,477 --> 00:30:34,516
which no less promises to make
me a true believer in magic.

633
00:30:34,551 --> 00:30:35,862
Although I must admit
the mere thought

634
00:30:35,897 --> 00:30:38,727
of such a thing being
real is intriguing.

635
00:30:38,762 --> 00:30:40,729
- That's your
garage door opener.

636
00:30:40,764 --> 00:30:42,145
- Oh, a warning.

637
00:30:42,179 --> 00:30:46,218
"Ye beware who layeth
sight on the pages within."

638
00:30:46,252 --> 00:30:47,322
[laughs]

639
00:30:47,357 --> 00:30:48,530
Nice touch.

640
00:30:48,565 --> 00:30:49,462
- But I probably
should get around

641
00:30:49,497 --> 00:30:51,568
to destroying Kozlak's hardware.

642
00:30:51,602 --> 00:30:53,639
- Must be a fuse.

643
00:30:54,709 --> 00:30:57,160
- Whew! Finally
got outta that car.

644
00:30:57,194 --> 00:30:59,783
- Okay, what do we have, here?

645
00:30:59,817 --> 00:31:02,061
- Merlin's light
summer recipes.

646
00:31:02,096 --> 00:31:05,754
- Contents:
Spells, Love Potion.

647
00:31:05,789 --> 00:31:06,686
Worthless.

648
00:31:06,721 --> 00:31:08,378
Teleportation...

649
00:31:08,412 --> 00:31:09,724
Hm, Rejuvenation.

650
00:31:09,758 --> 00:31:12,658
Ah, yes, we must
stay young and vital.

651
00:31:12,692 --> 00:31:14,246
- [laughs] What's his deal?

652
00:31:15,592 --> 00:31:19,527
- What kind of mind spends
hours writing this crap?

653
00:31:19,561 --> 00:31:21,494
Look at this gibberish.

654
00:31:21,529 --> 00:31:23,876
Typically, in Latin.
- Dumbass language.

655
00:31:23,910 --> 00:31:25,498
- Who was it that
first instilled a belief

656
00:31:25,533 --> 00:31:28,329
that words, perhaps
in their purest form,

657
00:31:28,363 --> 00:31:31,021
could actually
command the elements?

658
00:31:31,056 --> 00:31:32,195
- Uh, Bob Hope?

659
00:31:32,229 --> 00:31:35,957
- Take this spell, for
example, to propel away.

660
00:31:35,991 --> 00:31:39,443
"Derisera", oh!

661
00:31:39,478 --> 00:31:41,204
- The rug feels
soft on my back,

662
00:31:41,238 --> 00:31:42,412
and yet one can't help wondering

663
00:31:42,446 --> 00:31:45,553
whether extra padding
might not be called for.

664
00:31:49,488 --> 00:31:52,146
- That's what I get
for screwing around.

665
00:31:52,180 --> 00:31:54,769
Oh, hey, Miff.
- I have ear mites.

666
00:31:54,803 --> 00:31:56,219
[cat meows]
- All right,

667
00:31:56,253 --> 00:31:58,911
debating whether to continue
on with this foolishness,

668
00:31:58,945 --> 00:32:00,947
Jonathan Cooper
decides to play wizard

669
00:32:00,982 --> 00:32:03,916
in Name That Spell.
- I name it Fred.

670
00:32:03,950 --> 00:32:06,988
- Here's a good
one: "To Levitate".

671
00:32:07,022 --> 00:32:11,613
"Arisadare, Arisadare!"
[laughs]

672
00:32:12,925 --> 00:32:15,514
Look at me, I'm
the wizard, Merlin,

673
00:32:15,548 --> 00:32:19,449
the all-powerful sorcerer!
[cat meows]

674
00:32:21,382 --> 00:32:22,866
- It's time for a
strongly worded review

675
00:32:22,900 --> 00:32:25,420
of my cat, Miffy.

676
00:32:27,664 --> 00:32:29,873
- Doesn't he look like
Judy's husband, Punch?

677
00:32:29,907 --> 00:32:31,495
- Oh yeah, Punch.

678
00:32:31,530 --> 00:32:33,083
- Ooh, "To Summon a Spirit,

679
00:32:33,118 --> 00:32:35,534
"say three times in
a commanding tone,

680
00:32:35,568 --> 00:32:39,676
"Vien-e-chi-Re,
Vien-e-chi-Re, Vien-e-chi-Re."

681
00:32:39,710 --> 00:32:41,781
- Ah, a doratio!

682
00:32:42,989 --> 00:32:44,750
- Ooh, somebody put
tinfoil in the microwave.

683
00:32:44,784 --> 00:32:48,133
[coughs]
[fire flames]

684
00:32:49,479 --> 00:32:53,172
- Channelling the
spirit of a circus freak.

685
00:32:54,346 --> 00:32:56,417
[Servo laughs]

686
00:32:58,073 --> 00:33:01,560
- Now he can return
that arc welder.

687
00:33:01,594 --> 00:33:04,459
- Oh, l what am I saying?

688
00:33:04,494 --> 00:33:06,254
[dramatic music]

689
00:33:07,255 --> 00:33:10,465
- Oh, thank you, Latin.

690
00:33:14,676 --> 00:33:17,990
- Clearly, Merlin has
brought good into the world.

691
00:33:19,474 --> 00:33:23,616
- Those altoids are
curiously strong.

692
00:33:23,651 --> 00:33:24,721
[Madeline coughs]

693
00:33:24,755 --> 00:33:26,757
- Ed from next door came
over and got me pregnant,

694
00:33:26,792 --> 00:33:28,173
so everything's fine.

695
00:33:28,207 --> 00:33:31,106
- What on Earth is
going on down here?

696
00:33:31,141 --> 00:33:32,901
The lights just
exploded in the bedroom,

697
00:33:32,936 --> 00:33:34,558
nearly scared me to death.

698
00:33:34,593 --> 00:33:38,183
- My tongue's a curly
fry, can we talk later?

699
00:33:39,839 --> 00:33:42,670
- She's Julie Haggertying.

700
00:33:42,704 --> 00:33:44,085
- Say, that Merlin guy called

701
00:33:44,119 --> 00:33:48,538
and invited me down to
Barbados for the weekend.

702
00:33:48,572 --> 00:33:51,368
- Why are you
sitting in the dark?

703
00:33:51,403 --> 00:33:52,473
What are you doing?

704
00:33:52,507 --> 00:33:54,164
Are you trying to
burn the house down?

705
00:33:54,199 --> 00:33:57,512
- I utterly loathe you,
you wanna have a baby?

706
00:33:59,307 --> 00:34:01,965
- Jonathan, I'm sorry.

707
00:34:01,999 --> 00:34:05,140
I know it's been hard, but
we can get through this.

708
00:34:05,175 --> 00:34:06,625
I mean, having a baby...

709
00:34:06,659 --> 00:34:08,074
- That protrudes
my neck cords, so...

710
00:34:08,109 --> 00:34:11,561
- Hey, there are thousands of
childless couples out there.

711
00:34:11,595 --> 00:34:15,461
It's nothing to be ashamed of.

712
00:34:15,496 --> 00:34:17,222
We just have to stop
blaming each other.

713
00:34:17,256 --> 00:34:20,121
- Thanks, honey, I'm
glad I had this talk.

714
00:34:21,364 --> 00:34:22,882
- You haven't heard
a word I've said.

715
00:34:22,917 --> 00:34:24,850
- Chuck Woolery.

716
00:34:24,884 --> 00:34:26,196
- Leave.

717
00:34:26,231 --> 00:34:28,025
- What is going on with you?

718
00:34:28,060 --> 00:34:30,545
- This is weird,
you're usually so nice.

719
00:34:30,580 --> 00:34:33,272
- Jonathan, you're scaring me.

720
00:34:34,549 --> 00:34:36,827
- I'm taking the flashlight
and the Longaberger basket,

721
00:34:36,862 --> 00:34:39,692
that's all I need.

722
00:34:43,040 --> 00:34:46,285
- Damn, I singed my
Mary Engelbreit calendar.

723
00:34:50,255 --> 00:34:51,635
- "Dragon's Breath."

724
00:34:51,670 --> 00:34:53,534
- Clorets can help.
- It works!

725
00:34:53,568 --> 00:34:54,880
This book really works.

726
00:34:54,914 --> 00:34:57,469
- Unlike How to Meet Girls,
which did nothing for me.

727
00:34:57,503 --> 00:35:01,369
- So where's the spirit?

728
00:35:01,404 --> 00:35:02,888
Anybody there?

729
00:35:02,922 --> 00:35:04,890
- Come out, or I'll review you!

730
00:35:06,201 --> 00:35:09,239
- Maybe that wasn't
commanding enough.

731
00:35:09,274 --> 00:35:10,861
This is incredible!

732
00:35:10,896 --> 00:35:13,588
- Like that show
with Fran Tarkenton.

733
00:35:13,623 --> 00:35:14,589
- The homing spell.

734
00:35:14,624 --> 00:35:17,351
"Upon proper orchestration
of this incantation,

735
00:35:17,385 --> 00:35:21,458
"an object may be sent
away to later return."

736
00:35:21,493 --> 00:35:22,563
Like a homing pigeon.

737
00:35:22,597 --> 00:35:24,806
- Or a domesticated lobster.

738
00:35:24,841 --> 00:35:26,463
- Ah, this is what
Merlin warned me about.

739
00:35:26,498 --> 00:35:27,878
What did he say?

740
00:35:27,913 --> 00:35:29,880
"Don't toy with any spells
that aren't entirely there."

741
00:35:29,915 --> 00:35:32,504
- And something about
biting him, I think.

742
00:35:32,538 --> 00:35:36,784
- That old buzzard knew damn
well I was going to dabble.

743
00:35:36,818 --> 00:35:41,133
Well, far be it for me to go
against the master's wishes.

744
00:35:41,167 --> 00:35:42,341
- I talk to myself a lot.

745
00:35:42,376 --> 00:35:44,481
Long monologues,
complete with sarcasm.

746
00:35:44,516 --> 00:35:46,932
- "To Call Forward,
Vien-e-chi-Ra."

747
00:35:46,966 --> 00:35:49,590
- It's a phone manual.
- "Vien-e-chi-Ra."

748
00:35:49,624 --> 00:35:52,282
Thought that was
to summon a spirit?

749
00:35:52,317 --> 00:35:55,078
- Hey, there's how
install a baseboard heater.

750
00:35:55,112 --> 00:35:57,563
- Ah, the last
letter is different.

751
00:35:57,598 --> 00:36:01,464
- Typical Latin crap.
I'm glad it's dead.

752
00:36:03,120 --> 00:36:05,260
- Vien-e-chi-Ra.

753
00:36:05,295 --> 00:36:06,400
[bottle crashes]
